#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# wavelet_map_indexed

#% text
# `wavelet_map_indexed(f, d)` gives the wavelet data d (discrete or continuous) with every coefficient array c replaced by f(c, index) for a function of two parameters, by f(c) otherwise; `wavelet_map_indexed(f, d, sel)` changes only the selected arrays.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
d = discrete_wavelet_transform([1, 2, 3, 4], haar_wavelet(), 1)

#% cell
wavelet_map_indexed(c => 2*c, d)(all)
#% output
#= [[0] -> [4.242640687119286, 9.899494936611667], [1] -> [-1.4142135623730951, -1.414213562373095]]

#% cell
wavelet_map_indexed((c, k) => if k === [1] then 0*c else c, d)(all)
#% output
#= [[0] -> [2.121320343559643, 4.949747468305834], [1] -> [-0.0, -0.0]]

